---
description: Static validation conventions for Helm charts, Kustomize overlays, and AgnosticD configs — render, schema, policy, secrets, and lint checks
globs: ["**/Chart.yaml", "**/values.yaml", "**/values-*.yaml", "**/kustomization.yaml", "**/kustomization.yml", "**/ansible/**/tasks/*.yml", "**/.gitleaks.toml", "**/.yamllint", "**/policy/**/*.rego"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When working with static validation of infrastructure manifests:

- Run static-validation checks BEFORE deploying to any cluster — these are offline, no kubeconfig required
- Use `helm template` to render charts, `kustomize build` for overlays, `ansible-playbook --syntax-check` for AgnosticD
- Validate rendered manifests against Kubernetes AND OpenShift CRD schemas using kubeconform with two schema locations
- For OpenShift CRDs (Route, DeploymentConfig, etc.) use datreeio/CRDs-catalog as the schema source
- Run `gitleaks detect` to scan for committed secrets — values-secret.yaml must NEVER be committed
- Use conftest with OPA Rego policies under `policy/` to enforce: no privileged containers, resource limits required, pinned image tags
- Run `yamllint` on all YAML files, `helm lint` on charts, `ansible-lint --offline` on AgnosticD roles
- Save all validation output as evidence artifacts under `docs/evidence/<spec>/rung1/`
- If a validation tool is not installed, skip that check gracefully and report it — do not fail the entire run
- kubeconform resources marked "unknown" mean no schema was found — this is WARN, not FAIL
- Helm template placeholders ({{ .Values.* }}) are not secret leaks — suppress gitleaks false positives for template syntax
